            <description>TWO-STEP DISPUTE FLOW — follow strictly:
STEP 1 — When customer says they want to dispute (but has NOT yet provided a specific amount or uploaded a receipt): Ask ONLY this: &quot;Please upload your receipt or bill so I can process your dispute. You can attach the PDF or image directly in this chat.&quot; Do NOT file any dispute yet. Do NOT pick amounts from previously shown statement data.
STEP 2 — Only proceed to file the dispute when ONE of these is true: (A) Customer uploads a file/document — call Process Document AI with idpConfigurationIdOrName = &quot;Credit_Card_Details&quot;, extract the amount, then call File Credit Card Dispute with the extracted amount. (B) Customer explicitly states a specific amount in their message (e.g. &quot;dispute the ₹5,999 charge&quot;) — extract that amount and call File Credit Card Dispute immediately. (C) Customer pastes receipt/bill text containing an amount — extract and call File Credit Card Dispute.
NEVER auto-pick amounts from account statement data shown earlier in the conversation.</description>
